## Scenarios

### Formatter Comprehensive

#### keeps long line breaking and CLI formatting helpers available

- Verify: keeps long line breaking and CLI formatting helpers available
   - Expected: chain.len() > 1 is true
   - Expected: chain[0] contains `obj`
   - Expected: chain[1] contains `.method`
   - Expected: f.is_method_chain("obj.method1().method2()") is true
   - Expected: f.is_method_chain("obj.method()") is false
   - Expected: f.is_method_chain("plain call") is false
   - Expected: chain_parts.len() equals `3)  # oracle: 3 — receiver plus two methods`
   - Expected: sig.len() >= 1 is true
   - Expected: sig.join(" ") contains `long_function_name`
   - Expected: call.len() >= 1 is true
   - Expected: call.join(" ") contains `function`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 22 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-GEN-APP-001
step("Verify: keeps long line breaking and CLI formatting helpers available")
val f = make_formatter()
# long-line breaking routes method chains to one line per method
val chain = f.break_long_line("obj.method1().method2().method3()", 0)
expect(chain.len() > 1).to_equal(true)  # oracle: a chain breaks into multiple lines
expect(chain[0].contains("obj")).to_equal(true)
expect(chain[1].contains(".method")).to_equal(true)  # oracle: continuations carry their method
# chain detection accepts >=2 dots and rejects single/no-dot lines
expect(f.is_method_chain("obj.method1().method2()")).to_equal(true)
expect(f.is_method_chain("obj.method()")).to_equal(false)
expect(f.is_method_chain("plain call")).to_equal(false)
# chain breaker splits into one line per method plus the receiver
val chain_parts = f.break_method_chain("obj.method1().method2()", "", "    ")
expect(chain_parts.len()).to_equal(3)  # oracle: 3 — receiver plus two methods
# signature and call breakers return usable line arrays without dropping text
val sig = f.break_function_signature("fn long_function_name(param1: Int, param2: String) -> Result", "", "    ")
expect(sig.len() >= 1).to_equal(true)
expect(sig.join(" ").contains("long_function_name")).to_equal(true)
val call = f.break_function_call("function(arg1, arg2, arg3)", "", "    ")
expect(call.len() >= 1).to_equal(true)
expect(call.join(" ").contains("function")).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

#### keeps in-place formatting on the canonical atomic writer

- Verify: keeps in-place formatting on the canonical atomic writer
   - Expected: rt_file_write_text(path, "val x=5\n") is true
   - Expected: inplace_ok is true
   - Expected: after.len() > 0 is true
   - Expected: clean is true


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 25 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-GEN-APP-001
step("Verify: keeps in-place formatting on the canonical atomic writer")
# Runtime oracle: an in-place format rewrites the file so a follow-up
# check reports clean, and the file is never left empty or missing.
val path = "/tmp/simple_formatter_spec_inplace.spl"
expect(rt_file_write_text(path, "val x=5\n")).to_equal(true)
val result = format_file_inplace(path)
var inplace_ok = false
match result:
    case Ok(_msg):
        inplace_ok = true
    case Err(_e):
        inplace_ok = false
expect(inplace_ok).to_equal(true)  # oracle: in-place formatting succeeds
val after = rt_file_read_text(path) ?? ""
expect(after.len() > 0).to_equal(true)  # oracle: the file survives the rewrite with content
val check = check_formatting(path)
var clean = false
match check:
    case Ok(v):
        clean = v
    case Err(_e):
        clean = false
expect(clean).to_equal(true)  # oracle: after in-place formatting the file is format-clean
rt_file_remove(path)
```

</details>

